{"highest":5,"ids":{"RQREB-1 is not covered: DSRACE-1 covers concurrent-claim detection by reading back GitHub comments (notes), not by fetching the GitHub issue itself; \"reads back all trusted concurrent claim notes\" and \"re-reads the issue\" are different operations, and no SPEC demands that the issue's metadata or labels are read after adding the label — After adding the label, a run re-reads the issue [FIX IN DESIGN: ACCEPTED IF: a SPEC demands that after successfully adding the label, the claim reads back the GitHub issue itself (its data — labels, state, or metadata — not only comments or notes), and the read occurs after the synchronous holder record is written]":"DSFND-1","UNCLEAR RQCMT-1: the issue now answers it: the issue says the standard progress comment does not exist at claim time — it is started in the background after `pipeline.start`, which never fires for a refused run — so at claim time the arbitration note is the only GitHub comment the loser posts; \"marks its progress comment as not started\" therefore refers to that note — Today the progress comment is started in the background, after the issue lock (zbuild_issue_lock_acquire, core/pipeline/runner.sh) and pipeline.start, so at claim time a run has no comment of its own to compare [FIX IN DESIGN: ACCEPTED IF: the UNCLEAR RQCMT-1 line is gone, and the work follows the issue's words where they differ from its assumption]":"DSFND-2","DSRACE-2: 1 part to fix\nDSRACE-2[code]: Only the run whose concurrent claim note is first (by created_at, then id) returns {\"acquired\": true}; all others return {\"acquired\": false} covers: RQTIE-2, RQTIE-1\n  Given: two or more concurrent claim notes exist for the same issue within the detection window\n  When: each run compares the notes and identifies the first\n  Then: the run whose note has the earliest created_at returns {\"acquired\": true} and deletes its note [FIX IN DESIGN: the issue requires the first-claiming run to proceed; it says nothing about the winner deleting its arbitration note — ACCEPTED IF: the Then must state only that the winning run returns {\"acquired\": true}, without committing to any note-deletion step the issue does not ask for]\n  And: all other runs return {\"acquired\": false, \"holder\": \"<winner_holder>\", \"race_lost\": true}":"DSFND-3","DSRACE-4: 1 part to fix\nDSRACE-4[done]: A run whose claim_coordinator_claim returns {\"acquired\": false} never removes the zbuild:claimed label covers: RQLBL-1 evidence: core/claim/claim.sh | [[ -n \"$issue\" ]] || return 0 [FIX IN DESIGN: when `claim_coordinator_claim` returns `{\"acquired\": false}`, the existing code calls `_zbuild_claim_takeover` for any cross-machine holder (lines 119–123 of `zbuild_claim_acquire`); inside `_zbuild_claim_takeover`, if the takeover hook returns `taken_over: true, claimed: true`, the code sets `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED=\"$issue\"` (line 197 of `_zbuild_claim_takeover`), after which `zbuild_claim_release` will remove the label — so `_ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED` is NOT guaranteed never-set after `acquired: false` in the existing code; that guarantee requires DSRACE-5's `race_lost: true` skip to be in place first: core/claim/claim.sh | _ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED=\"$issue\" — it is [code], not [done] — ACCEPTED IF: DSRACE-4 must be [code], conditioned on DSRACE-5, with evidence showing the stale-takeover path is unreachable for a race-lost response]\n  When: claim_coordinator_claim returns {\"acquired\": false, ...}\n  Then: _ZBUILD_CLAIM_ACQUIRED is never set, zbuild_claim_release is a no-op, and the label is not removed":"DSFND-4","Decision: the design's decisions go against the issue: RQTIE-1 requires that when two runs claim an issue at the same moment, exactly one proceeds — no qualification. The design's outside assumptions explicitly describe a scenario where both competing runs complete their note-post-and-read cycle before the other run's note has propagated, both see only their own note, and both return `{\"acquired\": true}`. Both runs therefore proceed, which cannot be true together with RQTIE-1. — has propagated, both see only their own note and both return `{\"acquired\": true}`. Closing [FIX IN DESIGN: ACCEPTED IF: The design does not accept a scenario where both runs return `{\"acquired\": true}` and proceed; or RQTIE-1 is itself qualified in the issue to permit a narrow propagation-window exception.]":"DSFND-5"}}
